In the next 180-365 days, the strongest teams will build internal evaluation loops that replay closed tickets, compare multiple candidate diffs, and gate agent autonomy on quantitative thresholds such as pass rate on historical tasks and regression-free merge percentages. This makes directed software evolution practical because selection pressure becomes explicit and automatable: variants are not kept because they look elegant, but because they outperform a baseline under the same test harness. The engineering win is not just better ranking of models; it is continuous calibration of the whole agent stack, including retrieval, tool use, sandbox setup, and patch repair under real repository conditions.","step_at":"1","title":"Evaluation/testing direction: replay harnesses and CI-derived selection metrics become the default test bed for coding agents"},"timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:42:35.626462Z","to_status":"Proposed"}],"fields":{"Id":"en-019d95ab-c565-7d00-9bdd-40326b34720c","Status":"Proposed","counterfactual_summary":"If this is wrong, organizations will continue to rely mainly on external benchmarks and anecdotal developer satisfaction, which would imply that repository-specific replay systems are too expensive or too brittle to become standard evaluation infrastructure.","grounding":"[]","observation_ids":"["en-019d95ab-2bfd-7501-a5e7-61343258079d","en-019d95ab-4df2-73e3-b615-f4c5fdedc6ab","en-019d95ab-685a-7f31-b124-59f9ca94724b"]","projection_id":"en-019d95aa-b3d9-77c3-8da3-2d8b6860d48b","proposer_agent_id":"aj-019d95aa-b422-7a51-88d0-17960b62acc6","reasoning":"Evaluation/testing direction: enterprise adoption will consolidate around replay-based evaluation harnesses tied directly to CI and historical engineering work, not public benchmark leaderboards alone. Signals from ProdCodeBench, Sigmabench, and longer-horizon task benchmarks indicate that practitioners are already moving from single-turn correctness scoring toward measures that resemble production operatio